Fixes for running EKA2L1 from a frontend (Batocera).
Upstream: https://github.com/EKA2L1/EKA2L1/pull/916 (drop this patch once merged)

- 12bpp (4096-colour) textures repacked to RGBA4444 instead of relying on a channel
  swizzle, which Mesa freedreno ignores on RGBA4 textures (wrong colours on Adreno 6xx).
- N-Gage / EKA1 display depth read from the ROM header even without a wsini.ini
  WINDOWMODE (4096-colour games ran as 32-bit with an extracted Z drive).
- A game started from the command line gets the pad without a click on the display.
- Every bind of a key profile is kept: one phone key can have several sources.
- A command line launch exits with its app, instead of stalling on a black screen.
- The key profile is reloaded when it changes while a game runs.
- background-image-keep-aspect and screen-scale-ratio: draw a picture of the phone around
  the screen and place the game in it, like the Android screen profiles.

